  That names a shared session/user-state module and a storage mechanism — neither exists in this repo — plus consumers
  that don't exist yet. That's architectural, not bounded, so I'm stepping up to the full process: questions,
  approaches, a written spec for your review, then a plan. The ratchet only goes one way; I'm not going to implement the
  one-line version and call the rest future work.

  Two constraints I found that shape this:

  - [38;5;153mapp.js[39m is a plain script tag ([38;5;153mindex.html:13[39m) with no modules or bundler. [38;5;153msrc/index.js[39m and [38;5;153msrc/utils.js[39m use CommonJS
    and are never loaded by the page. So "shared across the app" means picking a module story for the browser side —
    there isn't one today.
  - Persisting a user identifier client-side is auth-adjacent. Anything in [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m is readable and writable by the
    user, so the stored ID can be a display/tracking convenience but must never be what the server trusts to decide who
    you are. I'll design to that line; tell me if your backend already works differently.

